            {
                "entry_id": "508a485c-56c5-3c76-aafa-2854e16e976b",
                "word": "molesteren",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d67c36d6-781d-3b19-a446-d7cbd05eb825",
                        "entry_id": "508a485c-56c5-3c76-aafa-2854e16e976b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand in elkaar slaan"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "746fe625-84dc-42b1-8624-e7d15a1bc17c",
                                "sense_id": "d67c36d6-781d-3b19-a446-d7cbd05eb825",
                                "text": "Festivalbezoekers molesteren politie: Tijdens een muziekfestijn met Nederlandstalige piratenmuziek in Wapenveld (Gelderland) hebben enkele tientallen mensen zich vrijdagavond tegen beveiligingspersoneel en agenten gekeerd. Een beveiliger werd mishandeld en ook agenten kregen klappen, aldus de politie. Het tumult ontstond aan het eind van het feest, toen feestgangers de tent moesten verlaten. Bezoekers kregen ”om nog onduidelijke redenen problemen met het beveiligingspersoneel”, meldde de politie. Ze hield elf mensen aan."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aeef08aa-c252-3546-9e4f-18a8276ce9ef",
                        "entry_id": "508a485c-56c5-3c76-aafa-2854e16e976b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets kapot maken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9389671a-7fdd-4a90-915f-02c0f8b817a6",
                                "sense_id": "aeef08aa-c252-3546-9e4f-18a8276ce9ef",
                                "text": "Vandalen molesteren ‘Warme William’. De beer Warme William zit niet langer op zijn bankje op de Brug in Brugge. Vandalen hebben hem afgelopen weekend lelijk bewerkt. Het beeld moest noodgedwongen weggehaald worden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdb78b03-2e2e-431e-9633-baa2276811a2",
                                "sense_id": "aeef08aa-c252-3546-9e4f-18a8276ce9ef",
                                "text": "Een 41-jarige man uit Almelo is woensdag in de rechtbank veroordeeld voor een voorwaardelijke celstraf van twee weken, voor het molesteren van een ruit in de Havenpassage en het beledigen van agenten. Ook moet hij de schade, iets meer dan 200 euro, vergoeden."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "386f3db9-909f-36eb-b602-52e235721282",
                        "entry_id": "508a485c-56c5-3c76-aafa-2854e16e976b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand lastig vallen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "945828cb-67b3-4d36-9faa-0402bf4b660e",
                        "source_entry_id": "508a485c-56c5-3c76-aafa-2854e16e976b",
                        "source_sense_id": "d67c36d6-781d-3b19-a446-d7cbd05eb825",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand in elkaar slaan",
                        "target_lang_word": "beat up",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beat up",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "730c0a75-9241-373b-8948-244ec8972b3f",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give a severe beating to; to assault violently with repeated blows."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d27273f-045f-46f3-91ac-b98edce285f2",
                                                "sense_id": "730c0a75-9241-373b-8948-244ec8972b3f",
                                                "text": "I got beaten up by thugs on my way home."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33be62fe-28b2-4cb7-ae38-1f737b72177f",
                                                "sense_id": "730c0a75-9241-373b-8948-244ec8972b3f",
                                                "text": "You don't beat people up, so that you can live in a society where nobody would beat you up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01526df6-ea91-45c2-bbf2-94ebb7b16fae",
                                                "sense_id": "730c0a75-9241-373b-8948-244ec8972b3f",
                                                "text": "If anyone wondered why the liner went straight at the panzerschiff, Fegen's reasoning was clear. The 11-inch guns could hit him at long range, but the short-barrelled 6-inch on his own ship couldn't range out quite as far. So, to start beating up Admiral Scheer, he had to get closer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d175ad3d-81ca-309a-9b77-67f599741784",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To wake up earlier than."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9242e2f0-d046-44e1-a784-999f6c036fc3",
                                                "sense_id": "d175ad3d-81ca-309a-9b77-67f599741784",
                                                "text": "I wanted to beat you up this morning and make breakfast for you for once."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To attack suddenly; to alarm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d6e3809-6c7d-4148-b82c-15a4f43de4e6",
                                                "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                                "text": "At breach of wall, or hedge surprise, / She shared i' th' hazard, and the prize: / At beating quarters up, or forage, / Behaved herself with matchless courage"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8b2ca4f-4894-418a-b3c8-3ef9d844d3c5",
                                                "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                                "text": "On this occasion, the diligent prior o St. Andrews assembled 600 horse, with which he assailed the French, beat up their quarters, intercepted their provisions, and cut off their straggling parties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba9a4af5-ff5b-458e-9fe0-73c2a7383b96",
                                                "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                                "text": "Our people are daily gaining Health Spirits and Discipline — the spade & pick axe throw'd aside — for the British Rebels to take up — they notwithstanding affect to hold us cheap and threaten to beat up our Quarters — if we don’t beat up theirs first which is in Contemplation, this in time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70067358-3e14-4c32-9991-f0d5d446019d",
                                                "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                                "text": "\"We know for certain that their army does not consist of more than three thousand men, including all sorts.\" Sir Henry Percy, on hearing this, was greatly rejoiced, and cried out, \"To horse! to horse! for by the faith I owe my God, and to my lord and father, I will seek to recover my pennon, and to beat up their quarters this night.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3697b5cb-59cf-4305-92a7-db9cdbad605a",
                                                "sense_id": "851d1938-eb0a-3d7e-8e92-511381868440",
                                                "text": "Pa Blanken tells me that the Japs beat up our camp a month ago and we have lost all our heavy gear and moved up into the hills - he does not know where. Hell! No casualties, however. [...] Our material losses were very serious. The Japs had found a rucksack containing all our money, our medicines, including all our vital quinine, a copy of our signals plan, and a number of maps. […] It seems probable that the Japs spotted our camp from the air. They certainly knew its exact position and came straight to it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1bf37a6-9674-3f14-8486-80ad8a30aaee",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause, by some other means, injuries comparable to the result of being beaten up."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3dc10c8-b81d-420c-b51d-f0efe594e4a3",
                                                "sense_id": "b1bf37a6-9674-3f14-8486-80ad8a30aaee",
                                                "text": "He [= a paraglider pilot] flew into a hill and beat himself up pretty badly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b76d4615-a2a1-393a-aac5-a32c98cfe56a",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To feel badly guilty and accuse (oneself) over something. (Usually followed by over or about.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "reflexive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19224131-b768-4e88-a1ad-1eeecc26408d",
                                                "sense_id": "b76d4615-a2a1-393a-aac5-a32c98cfe56a",
                                                "text": "Don’t beat yourself up over such a minor mistake."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3334249c-63e0-3efc-a438-e61e40cc2fb5",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make (someone) feel badly guilty and accuse (them) over something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bc1812e-5227-4ec6-a25d-f8d28a917cce",
                                                "sense_id": "3334249c-63e0-3efc-a438-e61e40cc2fb5",
                                                "text": "It's getting louder and louder\nEvery time I think about you, about you\nI'll be better off without you, without you\nI wish my heart would stop, wish my heart would stop\nBeating me up (whoa, oh, whoa)\nBeating me up (whoa, oh, whoa)\nBeating me up"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a18af23-f7e0-343c-92b2-afb568f7f5bf",
                                        "entry_id": "3af4c3a1-2225-3444-9595-6573dc2e9a96",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To repeatedly bomb a military target or targets."
                                        ],
